  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening Malaria Control and Health Systems in Somalia - Somalia (01-Jul-2015-31-Dec-2017)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Somalia, Malaria, United Nations Children&apos;s Fund (UNICEF)This program has the following goals: By 2017, achieve and sustain near zero (&lt;1% parasite prevalence) malaria prevalence within areas of historically low transmissions (Somaliland, Puntland and Central part of South Central.  By 2017, achieve and sustain universal coverage resulting in 50% reduction of malaria transmission in malarious areas of the country (Southern parts of South Central zone).  To contribute to an integrated health system in Somalia which will lead to an overall reduction in all-cause mortality. The objectives of this program are: By December 2017, at least 70% of people living in malarious areas recognize and take proper action to prevent malaria and seek treatment..  By December 2017, ensure at least 90% of the population in targeted areas, are covered by LLINs or IRS as guided by stratification.  By December 2017, increase access to effective malaria diagnosis and treatment to at least 80% of patients in public health facilities, including primary health units, and 60% of patients in targeted private facilities.  By December 2017, strengthen health system monitoring and evaluation, and procurement supply chain processes..  By December 2017, strengthen national capacity for malaria surveillance and epidemic response management.</narrative>
  </description>
